[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397541218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492#issuecomment-3397541218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492","id":3397541218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Kgl1i","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T13:29:06Z","updated_at":"2025-10-13T13:29:06Z","body":"What problem is this trying to solve?\r\n\r\nI'm slightly wary that modern c++ offers all kinds of impressive ways to produce unreadable code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397541218/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397552224","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492#issuecomment-3397552224","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492","id":3397552224,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Kgohg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T13:31:42Z","updated_at":"2025-10-13T13:33:08Z","body":"I'm also weary of hiding implementation behind macros and helpers and the risk of people getting used to using macros like this without fully understanding them, depending on the use case, or performance overheads of applying them incorrectly","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397552224/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397752722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492#issuecomment-3397752722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492","id":3397752722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KhZeS","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T14:24:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-13T14:24:29Z","body":"To me the code helps relatively little, it turns:\r\n```cpp\r\nI index = 0;\r\nfor (IteratorType itr = t.begin(); itr != t.end(); ++itr, ++index) {\r\n    T value = *itr;\r\n    ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\ninto\r\n```cpp\r\nI index = 0;\r\nfor (T value : Enumerate(t, index)) {\r\n    ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo me this would be entirely avoided if C++ allowed custom iteration steps in the for loop, like so:\r\n```cpp\r\nI index = 0;\r\nfor (T value : t, ++index) {\r\n    ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I think that for the specific cases where we want for-each iteration *and* index I'm not convinced the trade-off is worth it\r\n\r\nWould be good to get a feeling for how often this might be used, if we have a lot of cases like this where we want to iterate without random access (like when using `List`) or otherwise want the index and to avoid doing random access anyway\r\n\r\nWhen I did reworks ensuring no random-access to `List` there were relatively few cases like that, and the ad-hoc workarounds were relatively trivial\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\ntl;dr;\r\nI think this has to be weighed against the scope it would be helpful in, having a helper like this would IMO make sense only if it has many use cases and we expect to have a steady stream of additional ones in the future","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397752722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402097685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492#issuecomment-3402097685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492","id":3402097685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Kx-QV","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T14:13:34Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T14:13:34Z","body":"We could also go with a simpler alternative, and simply accept not unpacking the enumerated value:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nfor (Pair<const Value &, size_t> pair : enumerate(iterable)) {\r\n    // ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think this would accomplish a similar level of convenience without being as much \"C++ magic\".\r\nThat being said, I agree with the above concerns; if we introduce paradigms like this into the codebase, we should have a good reason for it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402097685/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432975343","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492#issuecomment-3432975343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492","id":3432975343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Mnwvv","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T15:19:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T15:19:29Z","body":"Is it much more work to add `ReverseEnumerate` (or `EnumerateFromTheEnd`)?\r\n\r\nIt would be super useful when iterating through lists to remove elements from them. Usually, we do something like this:\r\n```c++\r\nfor (int i = list.size(); i <= 0; i--) {\r\n    if (list[i] == whatever) {\r\n        list.remove_at(i);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd I recently stumbled on the issue of `uint32_t LocalVector::size()`, where it complicates really the logic of iterating backwards, because if your iterator is unsigned, it cannot ever be negative.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432975343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]